@jonathanhefner I see your 👀 on this. I have a possible fix in the works, but would be happy to chat with you about it. Basically I think if we make any reference to request.parameters before we get into routing we could get a 400 instead.

I threw in a new middleware to verify it would fix the problem and it does: https://github.com/rails/rails/compare/master...composerinteralia:check-params?expand=1. It might also make sense to incorporate a check into one of the existing middlewares, or directly into the routes app.

Feel free to take this over if you are feeling inspired 😄.
